{
  "case": "G50",
  "rule": "a cross hole's tool turns when its joint is made, so a member placed after assembly (after_assembly: a wall the frame is set against, a part fitted last, or a part on such a bar) does not cover its mouth then: of the faces that reach the core, the nearest no member covers wins, else the nearest only such members cover, a connection warning naming them (it cannot be re-tightened once they are in place); over a joint that itself joins a member placed after assembly every member counts. A connection may name the face per end, or per hole by its position, over the recipe's, judged as a named face is (after the decided frame's ninth run, F11, F12)",
  "design": "An 80x80 post on an 80x80 sill, a quick connector in each of two diagonal cores (Ø18 x 28 cross hole 25 up). A 40x40 frame member stands 2 off the post's +y face over the (20, 20) core; a wall 24.5 off its +x face is set against the frame after assembly. At (-20, -20): -y, clear. At (20, 20): +y is covered by the frame member, +x only by the wall, which is not there when the joint is made: +x, a warning naming the wall. The wall placed with the frame: no face clear, +y and an error naming both. Named +x by the connection at (20, 20): the warning; with the wall placed with the frame, an error naming it. Named +y: an error naming the frame member. Named -x for the end: -x at (-20, -20), and at (20, 20) a hole 60 from its core, an error and no hole. The wall turned to stand off +y with the frame member gone: +x, clear for good, over +y. A 40x40 fitted last in the wall's place: the warning names it. The post itself fitted after assembly: its joint is made then, the wall stands, an error. Each head bears 37.22 % under the sill's lips, a fit warning",
